Auroras by nimitz (@stormoid), 2017
https://www.shadertoy.com/view/XtGGRt

The shader's own header comment states its licence. Verbatim, the first three
lines of the file read:

    // Auroras by nimitz 2017 (twitter: @stormoid)
    // License Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported License
    // Contact the author for other licensing options

This was read in the copy of the shader at
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/y4my4my4m/kde-shader-wallpaper/HEAD/package/contents/ui/Shaders/Auroras.frag
(lines 1 to 3 of package/contents/ui/Shaders/Auroras.frag). That repository's
own GPL-3.0 licence applies to its own code and does not cover this shader,
whose header sets its own terms. The Shadertoy page itself could not be read
automatically (it sits behind a bot check), so the statement above is quoted
from the shader file, not from the page.

Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0
Unported License.
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/

This port (main.metal) is an adaptation of the original shader and is offered
under the same licence, Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike
3.0 Unported. It may not be used commercially. Anyone who shares it, or a work
built on it, must credit nimitz (@stormoid), link the licence, say that changes
were made, and share their version under the same licence. The author invites
contact for other licensing options; this port does not carry any such option.

Ported to Metal Shading Language for MacOS Live Wallpaper. What was changed
(the same list is at the top of main.metal):

  - mainImage's output parameter is declared as thread vec4& instead of out vec4.
  - Matrix products on vectors (v *= mat2) are written as v = v * mat2, and
    p*= -m2 as p = -(p * m2) (Metal has no unary minus on a matrix; same value).
  - gl_FragCoord.xy, used to dither the sample positions, is passed to aurora()
    as fragCoord (same value: pixel position, origin bottom left).
  - The pointer is replaced by the constant the original uses when there is no
    pointer, mo = (-0.1, 0.1); the slow camera sway is unchanged.
  - #define time iTime is replaced by iTime written out.
  - smoothstep on a vec4 uses vec4 edges, as Metal requires.

The maths, constants, step counts and animation speed are untouched. No images
are used. scene.json sets the render scale to 0.3 and the frame rate cap to
15 so the scene stays within the app's cost budget.

